# Next.js delivery boundaries

- Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only at the smallest interactive boundary.
- Never import server-only modules into the client graph. Props sent to Client Components must be serializable and minimal.
- Treat every Server Action as an untrusted POST endpoint: validate with Zod, authorize when authentication exists, derive trusted data server-side, invoke a use case, and return a bounded presentation result.
- Do not rely on client-side parallel Server Action dispatch.
- Create Route Handlers only for a real HTTP consumer. Use `Request`/`Response` only in delivery code.
- Pages, actions, and handlers must not query Drizzle or repositories directly.
- Use resource-oriented, kebab-case URL segments and clear dynamic parameters.
- Never change an existing URL without explicit authorization; report the breaking change when authorized.
- Use expected result states for validation/business failures and Next error boundaries for unexpected failures.

Read the relevant guide under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using or changing a Next.js convention.
